    {
      "id": "ja-t01.l2",
      "title": "One ticket, please: 〜をください",
      "canDo": "I can ask for a ticket or an item and say how I want to pay.",
      "intro": {
        "place": "station",
        "scene": "The ticket counter at the airport station.",
        "lines": [
          {
            "who": "レオ",
            "text": "すみません、{東京駅|とうきょうえき}までの{切符|きっぷ}をください。",
            "meaning": "Excuse me, a ticket to Tokyo Station, please.",
            "politeness": "polite"
          },
          {
            "who": "駅員",
            "text": "はい。{三千円|さんぜんえん}です。",
            "meaning": "Certainly. That's 3,000 yen.",
            "politeness": "polite"
          },
          {
            "who": "レオ",
            "text": "カードでお{願|ねが}いします。",
            "meaning": "By card, please.",
            "politeness": "polite"
          },
          {
            "who": "駅員",
            "text": "はい、どうぞ。",
            "meaning": "Here you are.",
            "politeness": "polite"
          },
          {
            "who": "レオ",
            "text": "ありがとうございます。",
            "meaning": "Thank you.",
            "politeness": "polite"
          }
        ],
        "notes": [
          {
            "title": "〜をください",
            "body": "Thing + をください = \"please give me…\". With no word for the thing, point and say これをください."
          },
          {
            "title": "お{願|ねが}いします",
            "body": "A softer, all-purpose \"please\". Use it with で for the way you pay: カードでお{願|ねが}いします, {現金|げんきん}でお{願|ねが}いします. It is the same で as {電車|でんしゃ}で, \"by means of\"."
          },
          {
            "title": "〜まで",
            "body": "まで marks where something ends: {東京駅|とうきょうえき}まで = as far as Tokyo Station. Add の to describe the ticket: {東京駅|とうきょうえき}までの{切符|きっぷ}."
          }
        ]
      },
