    {
      "id": "ja-t01.l3",
      "title": "How much? Numbers and yen",
      "canDo": "I can ask a price and understand amounts in hundreds and thousands of yen.",
      "intro": {
        "art": "💴🍙💧",
        "scene": "A kiosk on the platform. Leo is thirsty and a little hungry.",
        "lines": [
          {
            "who": "レオ",
            "text": "すみません、この{水|みず}{は|wa}いくらですか。",
            "meaning": "Excuse me, how much is this water?",
            "politeness": "polite"
          },
          {
            "who": "店員",
            "text": "{百五十円|ひゃくごじゅうえん}です。",
            "meaning": "It's 150 yen.",
            "politeness": "polite"
          },
          {
            "who": "レオ",
            "text": "じゃあ、{水|みず}とおにぎりをください。",
            "meaning": "Then water and a rice ball, please.",
            "politeness": "polite"
          },
          {
            "who": "店員",
            "text": "{全部|ぜんぶ}で{三百円|さんびゃくえん}です。",
            "meaning": "That's 300 yen in total.",
            "politeness": "polite"
          },
          {
            "who": "レオ",
            "text": "{千円|せんえん}でお{願|ねが}いします。",
            "meaning": "Here's 1,000 yen.",
            "politeness": "polite"
          },
          {
            "who": "店員",
            "text": "{七百円|ななひゃくえん}のお{返|かえ}しです。ありがとうございます。",
            "meaning": "700 yen is your change. Thank you.",
            "politeness": "polite"
          }
        ],
        "notes": [
          {
            "title": "One to ten",
            "body": "いち, に, さん, よん, ご, ろく, なな, はち, きゅう, じゅう. Tens stack up: {五十|ごじゅう} = 50. Then {百|ひゃく} = 100 and {千|せん} = 1,000, with {円|えん} at the end."
          },
          {
            "title": "The numbers that change sound",
            "body": "{三百|さんびゃく} 300, {六百|ろっぴゃく} 600, {八百|はっぴゃく} 800, {三千|さんぜん} 3,000, {八千|はっせん} 8,000. Everything else is regular. These five are worth learning by ear."
          },
          {
            "title": "AとB",
            "body": "Between two nouns, と means \"and\": {水|みず}とおにぎり. You met it after a person as \"with\"; the idea is the same, two things together."
          }
        ]
      },
